# The bundle's build scratch and download cache: binaries, never committed.
# `dist/*` rather than `dist/` so git still descends into the directory and the
# negation below can take effect.
dist/*

# Exception: the far-end bundle ships through the repo, so the second computer
# clones it instead of copying it over USB.
!dist/farend-bundle.zip

# Exception: the bundle's source record, written beside the zip by
# make-farend-bundle.sh and committed in the same commit as the zip it describes.
# Tracked text is what lets a check prove the committed bundle is not stale
# without unzipping it — see the grammar at the top of make-farend-bundle.sh.
!dist/BUNDLE-SOURCE.txt
